<li>Your policy, declarations page, and any roof-specific endorsements.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What a Thorough Roof Inspection Covers</h2>
<p>A carrier&rsquo;s first inspection is sometimes brief, especially after a large storm when adjusters are handling many claims at once. A thorough roof inspection usually looks at:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Every slope, not just one test square.</strong> Hail and wind damage are often uneven, with more damage on the side facing the storm.</li>
<li><strong>Soft metals and accessories.</strong> Dents on vents, pipe jacks, ridge vents, and gutters help confirm hail size and direction.</li>
<li><strong>Seal strips and fasteners.</strong> Wind can break the bond on shingles without removing them, leaving tabs that lift in the next storm.</li>
<li><strong>Decking and attic.</strong> Daylight, stains, and wet insulation show where water entered.</li>
<li><strong>Layers and material age.</strong> Multiple layers, brittle shingles, or discontinued products affect whether repair is feasible.</li>
</ul>
<p>Recording these details early creates a clear record to compare against the insurer&rsquo;s scope.</p>

<h2>Common Claim Issues and Insurer Arguments</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Age and wear.</strong> The insurer says damage is from deterioration, thermal cracking, or installation defects rather than a storm.</li>
<li><strong>Undercounted damage.</strong> A small number of hits in a test square leads to a repair-only scope.</li>
<li><strong>Matching.</strong> Discontinued shingles or tile cannot be matched, yet the estimate covers only individual slopes.</li>
<li><strong>Missing items.</strong> Steep or high-roof charges, starter strip, ridge cap, step flashing, detach-and-reset of solar or satellite equipment, and permit costs are left out.</li>
<li><strong>Pricing.</strong> Unit costs do not reflect local market pricing after a widespread storm.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our article on <a href="/how-to-review-underpaid-roof-insurance-estimate/">how to review an underpaid roof insurance estimate</a> walks through these items.</p>

